During development of the Corridor Prioritization Tool, our team met weekly with System Planning to track progress, review feedback received during the development process, and identify improvements to the tool. We also met monthly with district staff and users to gather feedback on the tool and better understand their needs. I incorporated this feedback into subsequent improvements to the tool. For example, when our team encountered spatial misalignment in APR data obtained for the analysis, I helped process the data to address the issue and worked with the relevant offices to confirm its spatial accuracy before integration into the tool.
